    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0957" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg807"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 160, of the 16th ultimo, reporting that none of the powers has
                    accredited <pb facs="0958" n="808" xml:id="pg808"/> a diplomatic representative
                    to the sovereign of the Kongo Free State, and suggesting that if the American
                    minister were so accredited more effective diplomatic action would result.</p>
                <p>In view of the action of the other powers, no change in the practice of the
                    United States in this regard appears to be necessary.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
